task: intent-multi-intent-measured
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/intent-multi-intent-measured
worktree: ../okay-wt-multi

why: the largest unbacked claim left in the module. `Span` has been in
  the type since the first lane and was the argument for why a flat
  label is not enough — "charged twice AND the app crashes is two
  spans, both to be acted on" — and THE FIXTURE CONTAINS NOT ONE
  MESSAGE WITH TWO INTENTS. The mechanism has never been exercised on
  a real message. Either measure it or stop claiming it.

  It also survives today's resolution finding: this is a binary
  question about whether a capability exists, not a two-point
  difference that sixty rows cannot resolve.

what:
  1. two-intent messages in the fixture, labelled with a SET
  2. measure what the SHIPPED no-LLM path does with them. It returns
     one label by construction, so the second intent is lost — the
     question worth measuring is whether it is lost SILENTLY or
     whether the cue tier's runner-up carries it
  3. the model tier's segmentation is the only thing that could
     actually produce two spans; a Live-tagged suite for it, run if a
     gateway is reachable and reported as unrun if not
  4. say plainly in the spec which tiers the multi-intent claim is
     true of, since today it reads as if it were true of the module

